+++ b/README.md
@@ -454,6 +454,18 @@ write, sync and close. Failed workloads cancel staging. Export failures fail the
 launch; an existing destination is preserved. Abrupt supervisor death can leave a
 private staging file, which is never a published archive. Consumers must require
 both successful completion and a valid archive. This is final export, without
-retained storage, checkpoint/restore, symlink or hardlink archive support.
+retained storage, live checkpoint control, symlink or hardlink archive support.
 Owned regular files support fsync/fdatasync against their supervisor backing;
 these calls do not imply persistence after the in-memory domain ends.
+
+`--restore-file <snapshot tar>` imports owned files before workload startup. It
+restores regular files, directories, permission bits and GNU long names into the
+new memory view. The current32-slot namespace (including prepared assignment
+parents), configured byte capacity and2 GiB archive payload bound all apply.
+The input must be a bounded regular file opened without following a symlink;
+import never changes it. Invalid paths, duplicate entries, links, invalid metadata,
+checksums/terminators and truncated data fail launch and discard the new view.
+The archive must have exactly two zero terminator blocks and no trailing data.
+This is filesystem reconstruction, without process memory, handles or matching
+runtime state; the host must select and verify the intended snapshot. It does
+not require a checkpoint control socket.
